ter(n):\r\n    \"\"\" emits 1 number per second  \"\"\"\r\n    for i in range(1, n+1):\r\n        yield i\r\n        await asyncio.sleep(1)\r\n\r\n\r\nasync def count_to(n):\r\n    \"\"\" counts to n in async manner\"\"\"\r\n    async for i in a_iter(n):\r\n        print(i)\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    loop = asyncio.get_event_loop()\r\n    tasks = [loop.create_task(count_to(3)), loop.create_task(count_to(4))]\r\n    loop.run_until_complete(asyncio.wait(tasks))\r\n    loop.close()\r\n```\r\n2. run `pylint asyncfor.py -d C`\r\n\r\n### Current behavior\r\nPylint reports that there is an error:\r\n`asyncfor.py:12:19: E1133: Non-iterable value a_iter(n) is used in an iterating context (not-an-iterable)`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\nNo errors for valid async for statements\r\n\r\n### pylint --version output\r\npylint 2.1.0\r\nastroid 2.0.2\r\nPython 3.6.6 (v3.6.6:4cf1f54eb7, Jun 27 2018, 03:37:03) [MSC v.1900 64 bit (AMD64)]\r\n\r\n### Note\r\nVersion 2.0.1 doesn't emit any errors for the same code:\r\n```bash\r\n$ pylint asyncfor.py -d C\r\n\r\n------------------------------------\r\nYour code has been rated at 10.00/10\r\n\r\n$ pylint --version\r\npylint 2.0.1\r\nastroid 2.0.2\r\nPython 3.6.5 (default, Jun 27 2018, 08:26:32)\r\n[GCC 4.9.2]\r\n```\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_